short-code {"wall_s": 30.910131374999995, "ttft_s": 8.991165415999998, "text": "Here's a complete Python LRU cache implementation using a doubly linked list and dictionary, with unit tests covering updates, eviction, and capacity one.\n\n```python\n\"\"\"LRU cache implemented with a doubly linked list and a dictionary.\"\"\"\n\n\nclass _Node:\n    \"\"\"A node in the doubly linked list.\"\"\"\n\n    __slots__ = (\"key\", \"value\", \"prev\", \"next\")\n\n    def __init__(self, key=None, value=None):\n        self.key = key\n        self.value = value\n        self.prev = None\n        self.next = None\n\n\nclass LRUCache:\n    \"\"\"Least-Recently-Used cache with O(1) get and put.\n\n    A dictionary maps keys to nodes for O(1) lookup, and a doubly linked\n    list tracks recency order. The head holds the most recently used item;\n    the tail holds the least recently used item.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, capacity):\n        if capacity < 1:\n            raise ValueError(\"capacity must be at least 1\")\n        self.capacity = capacity\n        self._map = {}\n        # Sentinel head/tail nodes simplify edge cases.\n        self._head = _Node()\n        self._tail = _Node()\n", "reasoning": "", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 59, "completion_tokens": 256, "total_tokens": 315, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 59}}, "finish": "length", "done": true, "temperature": 0, "case": "short-code", "thinking": false}
short-story {"wall_s": 25.045603124999992, "ttft_s": 4.831590916999993, "text": "The salt-crusted radio had been dead for three years, so when it crackled to life at 2:17 a.m., Elias dropped his tea. The voice was his own, only younger \u2014 brighter, unbruised.\n\n\"Don't take the boat out,\" it said. \"The storm turns at the last minute. I'm you, and I'm telling you: stay.\"\n\nElias gripped the desk. \"This is a joke. Hollis, if you're \u2014\"\n\n\"It's not Hollis. Hollis is why you're listening. He's the one who dies.\"\n\nThe tea pooled around his boots. Outside, the sea was flat as slate, the gulls quiet. Every instrument in the tower read calm.\n\n\"You're a liar,\" Elias said, \"or a ghost.\"\n\n\"I'm a forecast,\" the voice said, almost gently. \"I'm what you become if you go. I've been sending this message every night for eleven years. You never answer. You just leave.\"\n\nElias laughed \u2014 a dry, terrible sound. \"So I'm to believe a machine?\"\n\n\"You're to believe yourself.\"\n\nHe looked at the boat, then at the light spinning its steady beam. \"If I stay,\" he said slowly, \"who keeps", "reasoning": "", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 58, "completion_tokens": 256, "total_tokens": 314, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 58}}, "finish": "length", "done": true, "temperature": 0, "case": "short-story", "thinking": false}
short-reasoning {"wall_s": 25.78511108299999, "ttft_s": 5.843747332999996, "text": "Let\u2019s work through it step by step.\n\n**Given:**\n- Request rate: **120 requests/second**\n- Each worker handles: **20 requests/second**\n- Reserve: **25% of total capacity** for spikes\n\n**Step 1 \u2014 Required capacity without reserve**\n\nIf no reserve were needed:\n\n\\[\n120 \\div 20 = 6 \\text{ workers}\n\\]\n\nSo 6 workers would exactly handle the steady load.\n\n**Step 2 \u2014 Account for the 25% reserve**\n\nThe reserve means we should only use **75%** of total capacity for normal load, leaving 25% free for spikes.\n\nLet \\( W \\) = number of workers.\n\nTotal capacity = \\( 20W \\) requests/second.\n\nUsable capacity for normal load = \\( 75\\% \\) of total capacity:\n\n\\[\n0.75 \\times 20W = 15W\n\\]\n\nWe need this usable capacity to cover 120 requests/second:\n\n\\[\n15W \\ge 120\n\\]\n\n\\[\nW \\ge 120 \\div 15 = 8\n\\]\n\nSo **8 workers** are needed.\n\n**Step 3 \u2014 Check the result**\n\nWith 8 workers:\n- Total capacity = \\( 8 \\times 20 = 160 \\) req", "reasoning": "", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 72, "completion_tokens": 256, "total_tokens": 328, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 72}}, "finish": "length", "done": true, "temperature": 0, "case": "short-reasoning", "thinking": false}
